        "comments": "The assembly dcCerAlpi1.hap1.1 is based on 87x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species looks to be a allotetraploid, as we can see two different HiC patterns on the diploid HiC map, but it seems to work as a functional diploid. Haplotypic inversions were detected on: Chromosome 1 29.26 Mbp - 36.61 Mbp and Chromosome 7 37.55 Mbp - 41.26 Mbp.",
